{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/506808-silver-handcuffs","id":506808,"title":"Silver Handcuffs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-07T08:13:47-07:00","id":506808,"title":"Silver Handcuffs","content":"So I was browsing through V:tR 2E today and happened upon handcuffs. Apparently when in a grapple a successful overpower allows you to apply handcuffs to a person.<br /> <br /> So what does that mean for an Uratha in human form getting silver cuffs slapped on?<br /> <br /> Is this a minor 1-point aggravated while they shift up and shatter them off, or is this something more serious?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:20:20-07:00","id":506831,"title":"","content":"Probably 1 aggravated if they shfit up and snap them open, yes. But silver handcuffs probably wouldn't work especially well. They'd be heavy and less durable; probably much eaiser to break out of in the conventional sense.<br /> <br /> Also, werewolves don't need to shift up to get out of handcuffs: they can break their thumb and slip them off. Fifteen minutes later (or one essence) and their fine again.<br /> <br /> ADDITION: Or maybe shift down. Probably way easier for a wolf to just step out of the cuffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","user":"Full Time GM","date":". 05-07-2015, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:26:09-07:00","id":506841,"title":"","content":"Shifting down is probably the best option. <br /> <br /> Would simply having the bracelet on inflict the damage each turn? Instead of a handcuff, imagine hunters who try to snap a shackle onto you. Heavy duty steel lined with silver inside and out. What impact would this have? Could the Uratha &quot;play through the pain&quot; or are they going to writhe in agony from the constant contact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:42:53-07:00","id":506888,"title":"","content":"The Pure have a more severe reaction to silver; it would do a point of bashing each turn. For the Forsaken having bracelets of silver would be extremely painful but not damaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:45:19-07:00","id":506889,"title":"","content":"For forsaken there's no damage from just touching it. It <i>would</i> hurt like hell though. <br /> <br /> The Pure would be in more trouble, because they <i>do</i> take damage from contact alone. <br /> <br /> As for activity, uratha are mentioned to be able to use gifts at a 3 die penalty when in contact with silver. That implies that most other actions are doable, if difficult. Additionally there's a risk of death rage if any damage is done. <br /> <br /> Still, all this is why the Unchained facet is a good one to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T09:00:52-07:00","id":506904,"title":"","content":"On shifting down:<br /> I saw some Mexican wolves at the zoo recently and was surprised at how big their paws were. I'm not sure cuffs would just slip off a wolf unless the Hishu form had fairly beefy wrists. They're probably come off more easily, but not as automatically as you might think.<br /> <br /> On the silver-lined manacles, I think it specifically calls out that things need to be made of silver, and not just silver-plated to count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T09:04:07-07:00","id":506906,"title":"","content":"It works once, but then it rubs off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T11:33:34-07:00","id":507041,"title":"","content":"Pure silver, not plating and not an alloy. Lining the cuffs with silver doesn't do diddly from a mechanics perspective. Might be amusing to see a character who thought it would be a good idea find out otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T11:37:50-07:00","id":507044,"title":"","content":"If you really want to hold a werewolf you have to go further.<br /> <